{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me","id":914347,"title":"Explain Exigents to me","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-14T13:51:29-07:00","id":914347,"title":"Explain Exigents to me","content":"I don't know much about E3 and am curious about Exigents. I get that their the Exalted of lower gods, but how different from a typical Exalted are they. What does an Exalted of Parad, God of Inherited Might and Left Hand of Power look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:01:48-07:00","id":914353,"title":"","content":"Thematically, when a God grants the Exigence to a mortal, they are Exalted and gain powers based on many aspects of the God in question. Their powers may be themed after their purview, but also their personality, their appearance, and their history. I'm afraid I can't give insight into Parad because while I can make conjecture about what Inherited Might might do to someone's powerset, I know nothing about Parad in specific, so I can't color the powers in that manner.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, Exigents are &quot;build your own exalts&quot; toolkits. Literally it's design the Exalt you want to have, but based on the aspects of a God, not on a concept that a God could have as a purview. You never say &quot;Exigent of Birds&quot;. It's &quot;Exigent of Peyong, the Pecking One, God of Birds and Beaked Animals&quot; who is generous, but frugal. When you design the god first, the powers and aspects of the Exigent fall into place a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:34:28-07:00","id":914376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me#post914347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about E3 and am curious about Exigents. I get that their the Exalted of lower gods, but how different from a typical Exalted are they. What does an Exalted of Parad, God of Inherited Might and Left Hand of Power look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just spitballing here, but I imagine that they would have lots of Investigation, Lore, Bureaucracy, Socialize, and War based tricks. A perfect attack that targets based on Genealogy wouldn't be a far stretch of the imagination, nor would Persona charms that allow you to insert yourself into another person's bloodline.<br /> Just some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:56:05-07:00","id":914397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me#post914347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about E3 and am curious about Exigents. I get that their the Exalted of lower gods, but how different from a typical Exalted are they. What does an Exalted of Parad, God of Inherited Might and Left Hand of Power look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>So that's where all the Dynasty charms went!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:57:23-07:00","id":914398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me#post914347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about E3 and am curious about Exigents. I get that their the Exalted of lower gods, but how different from a typical Exalted are they. What does an Exalted of Parad, God of Inherited Might and Left Hand of Power look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be up to the ST and player.<br /> <br /> I know that's kind of a cop-out, but when coming up with Exigents, the two would need to work together to come up with a reasonable Charmset. My ideas for Parad might not be the same as someone else's.<br /> <br /> Just spit-balling here. If I were to make an Exalted of Parad, I would build them as something like the the main character from Assassins Creed. An Exigent of Parad would have the power to channel the powers, abilities and memories of their ancestors and magnify them through the lens of Exaltation because (Genetic Memory) or some similar BS.<br /> <br /> For Charms, I'd design their Charmset to be loosely based off the concept of the Persona Charms in the Socialize Charmset. When you first Exalt, you would create two or three ancestors and choose certain Abilities for them to favor. Then I'd play it off as inheriting that ancestors might and power. While you were channeling that ancestor you would gain access to Charms and powers that stem from that Ancestor's abilities. You'd be able to switch to a different ancestor, and gain access to their Abilities and Charms, but you'd lose access to the earlier one.<br /> <br /> As you gain experience, you can unlock more ancestors as well as level up your current ones.<br /> <br /> The same concept could be used for a god of reincarnation or whatever and just refluff it so that the Exigent channels the power of their own past lives (sort of like the Avatar from the Last Airbender).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-14-2016, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:58:58-07:00","id":914402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me#post914347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how different from a typical Exalted are they.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is a typical Exalt?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T17:32:50-07:00","id":914483,"title":"","content":"One important aspect of Exigents that hasn't been addressed yet is that the power to create these new exalted comes from the Unconquered Sun. A god petitions him for it, and if he deems them worthy, he grants them the Exigence, essentially a seed of exaltation which the god can then pour their power into. This is very draining for the god in question, enough to completely destroy many smaller gods, and greater ones will still find themselves diminished. Interestingly, the exigence can be traded or stolen before it is used (though this is very much forbidden) and even have multiple gods contribute to its power. These are &quot;black market exaltations&quot; and very dangerous.<br /> <br /> As for how different they are, that depends on the Exigent in question, due to how unique each one is. For more info in that regard, I'd take a look at <a href=\"http://www.avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Exigents\" target=\"_blank\">this page here</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Angel Toaster from Keychain of Creation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7935-cartographer7","name":"Cartographer7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7935_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:33:02-07:00","id":914524,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cartographer7</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914483#post914483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One important aspect of Exigents that hasn't been addressed yet is that the power to create these new exalted comes from the Unconquered Sun. A god petitions him for it, and if he deems them worthy, he grants them the Exigence, essentially a seed of exaltation which the god can then pour their power into. This is very draining for the god in question, enough to completely destroy many smaller gods, and greater ones will still find themselves diminished. Interestingly, the exigence can be traded or stolen before it is used (though this is very much forbidden) and even have multiple gods contribute to its power. These are &amp;quot;black market exaltations&amp;quot; and very dangerous.<br /> <br /> As for how different they are, that depends on the Exigent in question, due to how unique each one is. For more info in that regard, I'd take a look at <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalts#Exigents&amp;quot;]this</a> page here[/URL].</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it only gods? What about Kukla and 2nd Circle Demons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T18:41:05-07:00","id":914540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914524#post914524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it only gods? What about Kukla and 2nd Circle Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>By Word of Devs, it's only Gods.<br /> <br /> That said, meeeeeeh. :P I say if it's powerful enough and can get its hands on an Exigency, it ought to be able to make an Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:14:28-07:00","id":914571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me#post914347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about E3 and am curious about Exigents. I get that their the Exalted of lower gods, but how different from a typical Exalted are they. What does an Exalted of Parad, God of Inherited Might and Left Hand of Power look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <b>real</b> question is; &quot;What do you <b>want</b> them to look like?&quot; And there's no real wrong answer.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure the Kukla would <i>want</i> an Exigent, and I'm not sure what it'd do with one. I'm not sure that being able to depower the Kukla with Exigencies is a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:37:38-07:00","id":914584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914540#post914540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By Word of Devs, it's only Gods.<br /> <br /> That said, meeeeeeh. :P I say if it's powerful enough and can get its hands on an Exigency, it ought to be able to make an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's funny, because the Exigence appears to be the kind of thing that is usually given to the weaker gods; after all, it does seem to be basically defined as &quot;power bestowed on gods who, under any reasonable circumstances, would be to weak to Choose their own heroes&quot;; in a sense, being powerful enough to get the Exigence might almost be a contradiction.<br /> <br /> I think the main significance of &quot;the Exigence is only for gods&quot; is that it keeps the concept rooted in the society that is distinct to gods; it's not just a generic power booster for the purposes of calling Exalted, it is the Celestial Bureaucracy in action (as well as its distinct corrupt form).<br /> <br /> The Exigents aren't the only new Exalted around now, so I don't think the premise of a demon or the most powerful elemental in the world necessarily relies on it.<br /> <br /> After all, I'm fairly certain that the Chosen of some hole in the bottom of the ocean wasn't because that hole got bit of divine fire.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:47:13-07:00","id":914591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914524#post914524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it only gods? What about Kukla and 2nd Circle Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gods only. It seems like creating an Exigent takes the direct assistance of the Unconquered Sun and the process only works for gods. Elementals, Demons, Ghosts, etc, are out of luck. That's not to say you couldn't use Exigent rules for Charm creation and kit-bash your own version of Exigent Exalted that are created by Demons or Ghosts or whatever. They would just need to use a different process in order to Exalt their champion and they wouldn't be &quot;Exigents.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 06-14-2016, 11:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:56:04-07:00","id":914597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914524#post914524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it only gods? What about Kukla and 2nd Circle Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Canon</b> exigents are agents only of the gods, but it seems that one making up equivalents or &quot;DIY chosen&quot; created by adequately puisant beings like demons, elementals, fae, behemoths, hekatonkheire or less idenfiable entities through the use of the same mechanics would certainly be possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:19:44-07:00","id":914606,"title":"","content":"Great answers, folks. Do the Chosen still have the ability to exceed their makers? That was always a fun theme in Exalted. <br /> <br /> EDIT: and are we sure only Sol Invictus can create Exigents? Didn't the Infernals come into existence after a couple of the Primordials created their own Chosen and realized how it weakened them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:38:14-07:00","id":914625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914606#post914606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great answers, folks. Do the Chosen still have the ability to exceed their makers? That was always a fun theme in Exalted.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and are we sure only Sol Invictus can create Exigents? Didn't the Infernals come into existence after a couple of the Primordials created their own Chosen and realized how it weakened them?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was in the Infernal preview, so it might not be a thing once their actual book comes out. Assuming it remains, though, Exigency only comes from the UCS in canon so far. The Yozi just did not use the Exigency ( I doubt they even could do it, being mega-demons and stuff).<br /> <br /> Such mighty, great entities as Primordials, Incarnae, whatever the Dark Mother is and so on can make their own Chosen, they don't need the Sun's Exigency to do so. It is not using the Exigency that weakened them. Creating your own Exalted by any means would likely do so - much like the Sun set for the first time after creating the Solars.<br /> <br /> Also, yes, the Chosen can be greater than their maker. See that story in the end of the book, the tale of Strawmaiden Janest? You can bet the lowly field god who Exalted her through the Exigency wouldn't think they had any chance of a heroic stand up against a vast horde of Fair Folk.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:49:24-07:00","id":914632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914606#post914606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great answers, folks. Do the Chosen still have the ability to exceed their makers? That was always a fun theme in Exalted.<br /> <br /> EDIT: and are we sure only Sol Invictus can create Exigents? Didn't the Infernals come into existence after a couple of the Primordials created their own Chosen and realized how it weakened them?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Whatever those Exalted were, they're not Exigents.<br /> <br /> An Exigent is created when the Unconquered Sun bestows the Fires of Exigence on a god, and that god uses those fires to create an Exaltation. &quot;Exigent,&quot; is a very specific term that applies to an Exalt who was created by this process, which absolutely requires the participation of the Unconquered Sun. Without his assistance, the process cannot succeed. If an Exalt was created in any other way, they would still be an Exalt of some kind (obviously) but they would not be an Exigent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:50:36-07:00","id":914633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914584#post914584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny, because the Exigence appears to be the kind of thing that is usually given to the weaker gods; after all, it does seem to be basically defined as &quot;power bestowed on gods who, under any reasonable circumstances, would be to weak to Choose their own heroes&quot;; in a sense, being powerful enough to get the Exigence might almost be a contradiction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Powerful enough to USE the Exigency. IIRC it explicitly states that some gods are just flat out too weak to use the things at all. I don't have the thing to hand so I can't check right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914584#post914584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main significance of &quot;the Exigence is only for gods&quot; is that it keeps the concept rooted in the society that is distinct to gods; it's not just a generic power booster for the purposes of calling Exalted, it is the Celestial Bureaucracy in action (as well as its distinct corrupt form).<br /> <br /> The Exigents aren't the only new Exalted around now, so I don't think the premise of a demon or the most powerful elemental in the world necessarily relies on it.<br /> <br /> After all, I'm fairly certain that the Chosen of some hole in the bottom of the ocean wasn't because that hole got bit of divine fire.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Be that as it may, Exigence is the only method that I know of to make those things right this second. And honestly I like the one-off Exalt thing that Exigence creates. All the other examples we have are entire Exalt types.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:56:41-07:00","id":914640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914633#post914633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Powerful enough to USE the Exigency. IIRC it explicitly states that some gods are just flat out too weak to use the things at all. I don't have the thing to hand so I can't check right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll need to show a quote on that.<br /> <br /> The most that the Dev's have said is that Exigents (like all Exalted) are the result of a miracle and it can't always be predicted what kind of god can perform it and what will happen to it afterward. Even the weakest god could make an Exigent with only a slight diminishment in power, while a powerful god could be consumed utterly. Nobody can predict exactly what will happen. So while, in general, weak gods can't handle the fire without burning away (if they can handle it at all) and strong ones will only be diminished after making Exigents, that's not a hard and fast rule chiseled in stone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T21:11:22-07:00","id":914649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914640#post914640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'll need to show a quote on that.<br /> <br /> The most that the Dev's have said is that Exigents (like all Exalted) are the result of a miracle and it can't always be predicted what kind of god can perform it and what will happen to it afterward. Even the weakest god could make an Exigent with only a slight diminishment in power, while a powerful god could be consumed utterly. Nobody can predict exactly what will happen. So while, in general, weak gods can't handle the fire without burning away (if they can handle it at all) and strong ones will only be diminished after making Exigents, that's not a hard and fast rule chiseled in stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't exactly a definite statement, mate, and I did already say I don't have my book on me right now. Also doesn't invalidate anything else I said if I'm wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T21:43:18-07:00","id":914665,"title":"","content":"Do Exigents make their makers more powerful over time? That is the goal of the Primordial/Infernal alliance is it not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T21:58:56-07:00","id":914669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914665#post914665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Exigents make their makers more powerful over time? That is the goal of the Primordial/Infernal alliance is it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing has been said that indicates that an Exigent directly empowers their patron over time. Partially as the majority of Exigents lose their patrons in the process of Exalting. Though I suppose a few do just on the grounds of an Exigent being created to save a situation thus enabling the patron to still exist in the long run to regain their power. Other than that no we haven't heard anything that says an Exigent or it's actions will empower the patron. Chock up the Infernal thing as just a hope or an idea the Yozi have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T22:33:42-07:00","id":914682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914665#post914665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Exigents make their makers more powerful over time? That is the goal of the Primordial/Infernal alliance is it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>They might, but they very probably won't, and it's got to do with the name. &quot;Exigency&quot; means &quot;an urgent need or demand.&quot; There's a thing a god needs to do, something that needs a champion. Something that will take a large chunk of their power and being, probably, and that's not a light thing to give up.<br /> <br /> The Exigent could make the god more powerful, but that's secondary to the task that needs doing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11538-kingcrackers","name":"kingcrackers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11538_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"305"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T00:30:29-07:00","id":914707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914665#post914665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Exigents make their makers more powerful over time? That is the goal of the Primordial/Infernal alliance is it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the idea with the Infernals was to bypass the Law of Diminishment or something. Why sacrifice their own power when they can get a Infernal Exalt to a high enough power and then sacrifice their power to create a properly Yozi Exaltation.<br /> <br /> On the matter of demonic exaltations, if there where demonic equivalents of the Exigents, what would they be called? I would go with something like Facilic or Conmodian, from the English Facile and Latin Conmodus as words for easy or advantageous. This would be an opposite to exigent, which means urgent or difficult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T01:34:17-07:00","id":914716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914665#post914665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is the goal of the Primordial/Infernal alliance is it not?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGiven things the developers said about that preview in the weeks following it, I think the position that we have now (which is still several years ahead of them getting a book) is that the Green Sun Princes will have little to nothing to do with any Yozi plots to energize themselves and/or escape Malfeas.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigence is the only method</div> </div> </div> </div> What do the methods matter?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the one-off Exalt thing</div> </div> </div> </div> Then what's stopping you?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T04:55:56-07:00","id":914750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914665#post914665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Exigents make their makers more powerful over time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Inherently? Probably not, but if their patron's a god then they could perform actions that strengthen the god's purview which is probably why the official system requires the god in question to be virtuous otherwise most Exigents would be created to propel their creators into greater glories.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T06:29:10-07:00","id":914788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914524#post914524\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it only gods? What about Kukla and 2nd Circle Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know several people gave answers but there is another way to look at this that also answers your question on can creating an exigent make the god more powerful. Now I could be wrong but the reason Exigent are not created very frequently is the Law of Diminishment. For a god to create an exigent, they must permanently invest part of their power to create the exigent and it is possible if weak enough be destroyed in the process.<br /> <br /> I would think elementals and even 2nd circle demons would be unable or unwilling to permanently give away a portion of their power to the point they may not longer be what they were, it would definitely change them in a more drastic fashion than a god IMO. So while in theory a non-god could use an exigent exaltation, it would not unless the situation was so dire, they would be willing to be &quot;destroyed&quot; or rendered into a less powerful being.<br /> <br /> And thus the creation of an exigent would not make a god more powerful, so it is used in circumstances where the god MUST do something that for some reason is beyond its capabilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>while (horse.state == dead)<br /> {<br /> beat();<br /> }","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/830-amdramnar","name":"Amdramnar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T08:30:02-07:00","id":914848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=914716#post914716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What do the methods matter?<br /> <br /> Then what's stopping you?<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div>Levi. Please. Take it seriously. When someone presents a textual argument, don't obliquely quote rule zero. Rule zero always exists. I know rule zero. If I wanted to use rule zero to do whatever I wanted, I'd just do it. We're talking about why I'd open up Exigents slightly as opposed to writing entirely new things.<br /> <br /> You know the answers to your question already. Do YOU ever like having your arguments dismissed with the equivalent of &quot;it's an rpg, do whatever you want?&quot; It's annoying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T10:14:05-07:00","id":914899,"title":"","content":"But your suggestions don't seem to be about the Exigence itself, as in its already presented story context. You don't seem to be saying &quot;I want to tell a story in which a demon is tangled up in all of that Celestial culture and bureaucracy that surrounds the divine fire distributed by the Sun&quot;, you just seem to be saying &quot;I want a demon to use the Exigence because it's an already existing thing I can use&quot;, which feels odd to me because it seems to ascribe the setting an objective reality to be harnessed by internal actors, rather than an exercise in collective storytelling.<br /> <br /> Even if it's a matter of not wanting to deviate very far from the setting as it is already presented, that's the purpose of my pointing out other kinds of Exalted; that the setting already attributes the capacity for Exalted to come from places other than the Exigence. It's not rule zero any more than writing up your own Dynast or Guild factor is, it's just making the setting.<br /> <br /> That's apart from any argument I might make on how the ultimate origin of most Exalted is largely irrelevant anyway, and if the pre-existing notion of the society of the gods was not something that leant itself to the aforementioned stories of petitioning the Sun, then even Exigents could be something as simple as &quot;occasionally, a minor god will come out with an Exalt of their own, often in some time of great need&quot; and that's it.<br /> <br /> I think it's worth pointing these things out when so many people complain about the idea of the Exigence as just being for gods as though it constitutes something being denied to them, which really looks to me like getting hung up on an imaginary problem.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-15T15:40:43-07:00","id":915144,"title":"","content":"A demonic equivilent of the Exigence would probably warp how groups interacted with Malfeas as much as the Reclamation did.<br /> The one thing virtually all demons have in common is a desire to influence Creation, if there was a universal means to create Exaltation floating around Malfeas it'd consume the political situation there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-16-2016, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T04:44:44-07:00","id":915513,"title":"","content":"Another thing I've noticed, the Exigence seems to broaden a god's purview into thematically related areas so Strawmaiden Janest gets 'the harvest' rather than 'this field' so Ten Sheaves sacrifice mattered.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that Elementals and Demons should take the opposite approach, for example if Mara's the hypothetical patron then this should be about her and how she's a distinct being from Erembour and the Ebon Dragon rather than a proxy or an avatar because that's both reductive and a path to a watered down Fiend Caste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 06-16-2016, 07:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:19:37-07:00","id":915554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=915144#post915144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A demonic equivilent of the Exigence would probably warp how groups interacted with Malfeas as much as the Reclamation did.<br /> The one thing virtually all demons have in common is a desire to influence Creation, if there was a universal means to create Exaltation floating around Malfeas it'd consume the political situation there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Nothing would water down the nature of Exaltation quite like the Yozis making I Can't Believe It's Not an Exalt. A plot whereby a black-market Exigence is stolen and &quot;hacked,&quot; is a better one-off solution in that regard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T06:27:00-07:00","id":915557,"title":"","content":"That sounds a lot like a mortal Akuma, and there's a reason we pretend they were never even hinted to exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:04:22-07:00","id":915574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=915557#post915557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds a lot like a mortal Akuma, and there's a reason we pretend they were never even hinted to exist.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Even though I'm against &quot;demons hacked the Exigence,&quot;</i> there's a fair bit of difference between &quot;Exalt whose power is bestowed by a demon&quot; and &quot;mass-producible mind-raped slave with full-on Yozi Charms, whose power is bestowed by a demon.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sizable, even.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 06-16-2016, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T07:20:24-07:00","id":915586,"title":"","content":"Really, the way I see it first-circle demon using a black market exigence is simple enough and I don't really see any reason that wouldn't work. But the higher demons have that &quot;actually part of a yozi&quot; thing to contend with. If they diminish themselves they're going to be taking a chunk out of their progenitor, and the yozis have shown that they can already do that without Conky's help but disliked the results.<br /> <br /> So it could be that second and third circle demons <i>could</i> use exigence but are <i>forbidden</i> to, and you can bet their yozi would notice pretty fucking quickly if they tried to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T13:37:07-07:00","id":915812,"title":"","content":"I don't like drawing a line through the possiblity of Second and Third Circle Demons gaining their own exalts because of some edict of the Yozis but I think denying them access to a (relatively) convenient means to create their own Exaltation forces you to look closer at the demon and their methods.<br /> <br /> For example, Alveua would probably forge her hypothetical Exaltation as a physical thing upon the Forge of Night which would imply that it started out as a mortal of unique significance who gave themselves to be unmade on the anvil so who they were,why they did that and the form they took would flavour the end result and these non-Alveua elements to the design would be preferable to mining Erembour and the Ebon Dragon because they stem from her unique MO rather than who she's part of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T14:33:24-07:00","id":915846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=915586#post915586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really, the way I see it first-circle demon using a black market exigence is simple enough and I don't really see any reason that wouldn't work. But the higher demons have that &quot;actually part of a yozi&quot; thing to contend with. If they diminish themselves they're going to be taking a chunk out of their progenitor, and the yozis have shown that they can already do that without Conky's help but disliked the results.<br /> <br /> So it could be that second and third circle demons <i>could</i> use exigence but are <i>forbidden</i> to, and you can bet their yozi would notice pretty fucking quickly if they tried to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you're saying a second circle demon sacrificing itself is something the Yozis would instantly notice and forbid because it could weaken their progenitor in some nebulous way, but all those other ways second circle demons can and are killed by the crushing system of brutality that is living in hell, those are just fine? You'd think that if the Yozis didn't want second circle demons dying, Malfeas would either not grind his layers together, Adorjan wouldn't go 'round killing indiscriminately when silence fell, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T15:26:11-07:00","id":915874,"title":"","content":"I could see there as being a substantial difference to the Essence of whomever is next up in the chain between dying mundanely and sacrificing yourself to create one of the Exalted.<br /> \u200b<br /> And by &quot;mundanely&quot;, I even mean being permanently killed by something like Ghost-Eating Technique (although that could be another thing that scars the hierarchy); being crushed by the stone rain or slain in the usual intrigues of Hell is almost definitely the kind of thing that Second and Third Circle Demons can come back from.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that I necessarily agree with the idea of demons not using Exigence because they're forbidden, but I'll still grant those points.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-16T15:47:54-07:00","id":915891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=915846#post915846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you're saying a second circle demon sacrificing itself is something the Yozis would instantly notice and forbid because it could weaken their progenitor in some nebulous way, but all those other ways second circle demons can and are killed by the crushing system of brutality that is living in hell, those are just fine? You'd think that if the Yozis didn't want second circle demons dying, Malfeas would either not grind his layers together, Adorjan wouldn't go 'round killing indiscriminately when silence fell, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Second Circles don't tend to die due to the ambient conditions of Malfeas. They have the power, influence, and wherewithal to stay out of the way. That's doesn't save them from being <i>deliberately</i> killed by each other or one of their betters or <i>very occasionally</i> running afoul of Hell's violent nature, but Hell would be a silly place if Second Circles just up and died all the time. If two layers are about to crush Octavian's palace, you can expect he'll up stakes and move rather than being squashed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 06-16-2016, 06:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T01:14:25-07:00","id":916072,"title":"","content":"Well second circles are capable of reforming after death. You have to pull some extra tricks to perma kill a 2nd circle. So even if it were reasonable for The Hammer of Night's Forge to accidentally end up squished by a building collapsing under the shifting of the plates that make up Malfeas, it wouldn't leave the second circle permanently dead or diminished unlike the amount of power it would need to give up to make an exigence function. (If we're operating off the idea that someone managed to crack an Exigence to enable a demon to catalyze it.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T03:53:39-07:00","id":916111,"title":"","content":"Yes, there is absolutely no way Second Circles are subject to that sort of happenstance. Octavian has his empire, Berengiere watches over a certain graveyard, Alveua has the Forge of the Night. All those are very much physical places they lord over, and they are noted to having done so for a long time. The descriptions of Hell are colorful, but they are by and large for First Circles and other visitors; Second Circle Demons are great lords of hell, not its subjects, each one of the parts of one of its Gods. You don't watch them running away scared, you walk into their great palace.<br /> <br /> (Though, on the topic of the thread, I really don't see Demons making Exalted like that. Their themes and styles are too dissimilar, their ethos is different. I could see them making -something- that is PC-styled, but not in the model of the Exalted.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 06-17-2016, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T05:13:36-07:00","id":916132,"title":"","content":"I believe descriptions of the stone rain and Adorjan in Games of Divinity include references to them being threats to citizens as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:46:18-07:00","id":916194,"title":"","content":"I seem to remember a story about a massive Behemoth smashing up Sigreth's home. Second Circle Demons are powerful, but there are bigger fish in Malfeas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T07:09:10-07:00","id":916809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=915513#post915513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to me that Elementals and Demons should take the opposite approach, for example if Mara's the hypothetical patron then this should be about her and how she's a distinct being from Erembour and the Ebon Dragon rather than a proxy or an avatar because that's both reductive and a path to a watered down Fiend Caste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mara is a really tricky one because she is already very in line with The Ebon Dragon.<br /> I guess I would use the inauspious aspects of the House of Serenity as the primary inspiration for her charms and keep in mind that as the creator of Black Claw Style that she is a subtle fighter that employs misdirection. Its... something at least, if I was really going to attempt this I would have to work in more of my headcanon version of Mara for inspiration.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/535-bastet","name":"Bastet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T10:45:43-07:00","id":916903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/914347-explain-exigents-to-me?p=916111#post916111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, there is absolutely no way Second Circles are subject to that sort of happenstance. Octavian has his empire, Berengiere watches over a certain graveyard, Alveua has the Forge of the Night. All those are very much physical places they lord over, and they are noted to having done so for a long time. The descriptions of Hell are colorful, but they are by and large for First Circles and other visitors; Second Circle Demons are great lords of hell, not its subjects, each one of the parts of one of its Gods. You don't watch them running away scared, you walk into their great palace.<br /> <br /> (Though, on the topic of the thread, I really don't see Demons making Exalted like that. Their themes and styles are too dissimilar, their ethos is different. I could see them making -something- that is PC-styled, but not in the model of the Exalted.)</div> </div> </div> </div>While Octavian has his empire, i think CoCD: Malfeas mentions at least one 2nd Circle Demon, Tegus, the Ninefold General, that lost its kingdom and most of his armies to nothing more complex than layers of the demon realm moving &amp; clashing, leading to rent the remnants of his army as a mercenary company while he recoups resources &amp; contacts and looks for a promising place to eventually take over and start anew upon.<br /> <br /> About 2nd circle demons and Exalted, Alveua is one that i can kind of see trying such a thing at least, out of beliefs in her personal capacity to remake that which the gods made in more orderly and Yozi-pleasing forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}